## Notes
- Visibility groups (`performance.show_network_{wired,wireless,vpn,virtual,other}`) are applied by the engine or UI from `IfaceKind`; the mapping for Bridge, USB network and Cellular is open item E04-OI-9.
- Multipass bridges (PERF-004) need a name pattern the docs do not give; open item E04-OI-10.
- Build rule: run every cargo command through `flock -w 7200 "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/heavy-build.lock" systemd-run --user --scope --quiet --collect --slice=builds.slice -p MemoryHigh=16G -p MemoryMax=18G -p MemorySwapMax=2G -p OOMPolicy=kill env CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo ...`, for example `... cargo test -p tl-collect` and `... cargo clippy -p tl-collect --all-targets -- -D warnings`. Run `cargo fmt --check` too.
- `tl-collect` has no async code, no runtime and no `unsafe` (ADR-001 rules 3 and 4). No `unwrap()` or `expect()` outside tests (`clippy::unwrap_used` is `warn` and CI runs clippy with `-D warnings`).
- Read `CLAUDE.md` first. Commit once with a pathspec: `git add <your files> && git commit -m "<plan key>: ..." -- <your files>`. Never a bare `git commit`.

## Context
Turns the empty `tl-collect` skeleton from E02-A1 into a crate with its dependency list, its module tree and its error type. Every later E04, E05 and E06 bead edits only its own module file, so this bead writes every E04 `mod` line up front and creates one-line stub files. Sources: ADR-001 (allowed dependencies, rule 3), ADR-015 (`CollectError` via `thiserror`), ADR-016 (module layout, "Restricted, not zero"), R-135, epic map section 2.

