## Context
Graph data is a ring of 16-byte samples per series, owned by the engine reducer, and published as an immutable chronological copy (`SeriesView`) that the UI chart reads (ADR-003 "Series"). Flags mark gaps, counter resets and stale publishes so the chart never joins across a suspend, a restart or a device re-plug (PERF-022, ADR-008). This bead writes the sample type, the flags, the fast-tier ring and the view. The 1 Hz tier is E03-007. Sources: ADR-003 "Series", ADR-008 (counter and suspend rules), PERF-016, PERF-017, PERF-022, R-016, R-051.

